| **Thermal scanning** | The bot runs near-zero-power reversible logic or remains dormant 99.9% of the time. Its active phase generates less heat than a grain of sand absorbing sunlight. It matches ambient. |
| **Electromagnetic scanning** | No radio. No processor emissions. No electrical activity detectable at range. If vacuum-based logic is used, even near-field EM is zero. |
| **RADAR / LIDAR** | The bot's body is shaped and composed to match the surrounding sand or rock. Ceramic, not metal. Rough, not smooth. It's a false negative on every scan. |
| **Chemical sniffing** | The bot is sealed. It does not outgas. It doesn't excrete metabolic byproducts. Dormant, it is chemically inert. |
| **Anomaly detection AI** | The pursuer's AI is trained on "normal desert." The bot, its behavior, and its dormant construction process (subterranean, slow, ambient-temperature) produce no anomaly. The AI sees empty desert. |
| **Random sweep / grid search** | If a pursuer physically picks up the exact grain of sand that is the bot, the bot is caught. But the pursuer cannot find the next one. There is no signal to home in on. Each capture is a blind, random event. The swarm loses one grain of sand out of a trillion. |
| **Captured bot analysis** | The bot self-dissolves on capture (a pre-loaded, passive chemical cascade triggered by separation from the swarm environment or by a sudden change in physical orientation). The pursuer gets inert dust. No readable memory. No clues about the swarm's size, location, or purpose. |
| **Decapitation strike** | There is no leader. No central node. No "queen." Destroying a thousand bots doesn't slow the remaining million. They don't know the others died. |

**The Survival Equation:**

A zero-signal swarm in contested territory wins by making the search space infinite. The enemy is hunting for a single anomalous grain of sand in a desert, where that grain doesn't move, doesn't talk, doesn't heat up, and turns to dust if picked up.

It's not a military engagement. It's a war of attrition between a search algorithm and entropy. And entropy has more time.

