| **3. Vacuum** | Casimir-effect plates | Shared vacuum gap modulation | Communication channel is physically unjammable, but still a channel for spoofing. | Near-zero EM/thermal. Fragile hardware. Proximity-limited. |
| **4. Zero-Signal** | Immutable physical state machine | **None** | **No attack surface. No channel. No writable memory. No OS. No API.** | **Indistinguishable from the environment. Self-dissolving on capture. No leader.** |

The endpoint of the evolution is not a better weapon. It's not a faster computer. It's a system that has engineered out the very concept of an attack. You can't hack it because there's nothing to connect to. You can't hunt it because there's nothing to track. You can't kill it because it was never alive as a single entity.

That's the supercedent. Not a new technology. A new category of existence."

